  "description": "Reid Quest 2 SO 350W eBike | Electric bike\nPowerful, capable and built for bigger adventures – an electric bike designed for confident commuting, longer rides and exploring light trails.\nThe Reid Quest 2 SO 350W eBike combines a powerful mid-drive motor with a high-capacity battery and versatile components, making it a capable choice for everyday journeys, challenging climbs and exploring further afield.\nIts advanced alloy frame features internal cable routing and an integrated 48V 672Wh battery, providing a clean, streamlined design with balanced handling and plenty of battery capacity for longer rides. An Ananda 350W 48V mid-motor delivers powerful electric assistance, with 100Nm of torque to help tackle steep climbs and demanding routes. The Ananda Bluetooth display keeps essential ride information within easy reach and offers app compatibility.\nThe Uding D5 suspension fork provides 100mm of travel with hydraulic lockout, helping absorb bumps and vibrations across uneven surfaces while allowing riders to lock the suspension when a firmer setup is preferred.\nAn 8-speed Shimano drivetrain, featuring a Shimano rear derailleur and 11-32T cassette, provides a practical range of gearing for varied routes. The Ananda 170mm 38T chainset completes the setup, while Tektro hydraulic disc brakes with 180mm rotors deliver dependable stopping power and controlled braking.\nKenda 27.5 x 2.35-inch tyres offer grip, stability and comfort across urban roads, cycle paths and light trails. Completing the setup are 700mm alloy riser handlebars, an adjustable 80mm stem, a Comfort Plus saddle and ergonomic lock-on grips, creating a relaxed and supportive riding position.\nThe Quest 2 SO 350W eBike is ideal for:\n\nEveryday commuters, with powerful electric assistance for regular journeys\n\nRiders tackling steep hills and challenging climbs, with a 350W Ananda mid-motor delivering 100Nm of torque\n\nLonger rides and adventures, supported by a high-capacity 672Wh battery\n\nLight trail exploration, with a 100mm Uding D5 suspension fork and grippy Kenda tyres\n\nRiders wanting straightforward gearing, with an 8-speed Shimano drivetrain and 11-32T cassette\n\nRiders who value reliable braking, with Tektro hydraulic disc brakes and 180mm rotors\n\nComfort-focused cyclists, with 700mm riser handlebars, an adjustable stem and ergonomic lock-on grips\n\nPlease make sure to familiarise yourself with eBike and eScooter safety information before charging or using your new Reid. You can view and download user manuals and safety instructions here.",
